  "content": {
    "text": "CONCLUDED\n12 hours ago\nApple's new iOS 27 will work on devices as far back as the iPhone 11\nApple announced its new iOS 27 operating system on Monday, while disclosing that it will be supported on devices going back to the iPhone 11. That phone debuted in 2019.\nThe company typically makes iPhone software compatible with several generations of older devices. Eventually, older iPhones no longer support new software updates, at which point users may be motivated to upgrade their phones. Apple said that iOS 27 will work with the widest array of iPhones in the company's history.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "CONCLUDED",
